WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:04.810
These days, we're pretty constantly bombarded
with trailers, posters and other promotional

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:09.380
material for new releases in major, long-running
franchises but there also happen to be a few

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:11.700
part-twos that have managed to stay under
the radar.

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:16.040
From terrifying shark encounters to fascinating
murder mysteries, let's take a look at some

00:00:18.798 --> 00:00:22.978
It's been over five years since the men in
black last saved Earth from an alien threat,

00:00:22.978 --> 00:00:26.338
but now Sony plans on bringing the iconic
agents back to theaters.

00:00:26.338 --> 00:00:30.198
According to Deadline, the studio has their
latest entry in the Men in Black franchise

00:00:30.198 --> 00:00:35.858
set for release on June 14th, 2019, but don't
expect to see Will Smith or Tommy Lee Jones

00:00:35.858 --> 00:00:36.358
returning.

00:00:36.598 --> 00:00:39.258
Instead, the film will focus on a new cast
of characters.

00:00:39.478 --> 00:00:43.918
As Deadline explains, the studio wants to
produce a spinoff which can reboot and expand

00:00:43.918 --> 00:00:47.298
the franchise in the same way that Jurassic
World did a few years earlier.

00:00:47.758 --> 00:00:52.838
This sci-fi comedy will feature Thor: Ragnarok
stars Chris Hemsworth and Tessa Thompson,

00:00:52.838 --> 00:00:55.238
alongside returning MiB vet Emma Thompson.

00:00:55.678 --> 00:00:58.258
Mark your calendars and try not to forget
it’s happening.

00:00:58.478 --> 00:01:00.658
“Uh, ladies and gentleman if you would look
right here.”

00:01:02.078 --> 00:01:03.078
Death on the Nile

00:01:03.418 --> 00:01:08.237
While it may have received mixed reviews from
critics, 2017’s Murder on the Orient Express

00:01:08.237 --> 00:01:13.807
killed it at the box office, earning a worldwide
total of $339 million against a production

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:15.978
budget of $55 million.

00:01:16.158 --> 00:01:19.998
With that kind of cash, it makes total sense
that Hercule Poirot and his epic facial hair

00:01:19.998 --> 00:01:21.998
will be making a return to the silver screen.

00:01:22.478 --> 00:01:26.398
Only this time, instead of taking a train
ride across the wintry European landscape,

00:01:26.398 --> 00:01:28.638
he'll be taking a boat ride through the deserts
of Egypt.

00:01:28.758 --> 00:01:32.998
“Ah, mon ami, encore.”

00:01:34.278 --> 00:01:38.397
According to Deadline, Agatha Christie fans
can expect to see Death on the Nile sailing

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:40.958
into theaters on December 20th, 2019.

00:01:41.038 --> 00:01:45.858
Based on the 1973 novel, this new adventure
will follow Poirot as he tries to solve a

00:01:45.858 --> 00:01:48.318
murder on a riverboat that's cruising down
the Nile.

00:01:48.698 --> 00:01:52.218
It looks like Kenneth Branagh will both direct
and play the mustachioed detective, although

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:55.398
we don't know yet who’ll be filling out
the rest of the cast.

00:01:55.718 --> 00:01:58.658
However, we do know that Michael Green will
be writing the screenplay.

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:03.858
Not only did he pen Orient Express, but he
also wrote Logan, Blade Runner 2049 and all

00:02:03.858 --> 00:02:05.698
eight episodes of American Gods.

00:02:05.698 --> 00:02:07.498
Talk about a safe pair of hands.

00:02:08.138 --> 00:02:09.038
Zombieland 2

00:02:09.938 --> 00:02:13.938
It's been almost a decade since Zombieland
staggered into theaters, earning rave reviews

00:02:13.938 --> 00:02:16.198
and over $100 million worldwide.

00:02:16.458 --> 00:02:21.338
Since then, the movie has only grown in popularity,
with fans positively clamouring to see Columbus,

00:02:21.338 --> 00:02:24.018
Tallahassee, Wichita, and Little Rock back
in action.

00:02:24.438 --> 00:02:28.498
While there's been talk of making a part two
for quite some time, the film was never able

00:02:28.507 --> 00:02:33.397
to come to life but now, according to The
Hollywood Reporter, a sequel is finally rising

00:02:33.398 --> 00:02:34.618
up from development hell.

00:02:34.938 --> 00:02:40.178
Zombieland 2 is set to hit theaters in October
2019, and it's bringing pretty much everyone

00:02:40.178 --> 00:02:42.078
from the first movie back to the big screen.

00:02:42.578 --> 00:02:47.458
Jesse Eisenberg, Woody Harrelson, Emma Stone,
and Abigail Breslin are all returning, as

00:02:47.478 --> 00:02:49.558
is original director Ruben Fleischer.

00:02:49.838 --> 00:02:53.558
Paul Wernick and Rhett Reese who penned the
first film, not to mention both Deadpool movies

00:02:53.567 --> 00:02:55.097
are also coming back.

00:02:55.098 --> 00:02:59.118
We don't exactly know the plot yet, but THR
says our heroes will go, quote:

00:02:59.318 --> 00:03:03.478
"...from the White House to the American heartland
as they face off against new kinds of zombies

00:03:03.478 --> 00:03:07.418
that have evolved since the first movie, as
well as some new human survivors."

00:03:07.598 --> 00:03:11.068
They'll also have to learn how to get along
with one another as they make a new life for

00:03:11.068 --> 00:03:15.918
themselves in a zombie-filled, Twinkie-less
world — which is way easier said than done.

00:03:17.538 --> 00:03:19.658
“You might wanna buckle up, you know, for
safety.

00:03:19.658 --> 00:03:22.658
I can tell already you are gonna get on my
nerves.”

00:03:25.558 --> 00:03:27.458
What if you were forced to relive the same

00:03:27.468 --> 00:03:31.968
day over and over again, Groundhog Day style,
and were always killed at the end of it by

00:03:31.968 --> 00:03:33.638
some mysterious slasher villain?

00:03:34.138 --> 00:03:37.798
Naturally, you'd want to discover the identity
of your masked attacker and somehow break

00:03:37.798 --> 00:03:38.718
that vicious cycle.

00:03:38.998 --> 00:03:42.898
Written and directed by Christopher Landon
and starring Jessica Rothe as the oft-murdered

00:03:42.898 --> 00:03:49.698
lead Tree, 2017's Happy Death Day was a surprise
hit, raking in $122 million worldwide.

00:03:50.078 --> 00:03:54.178
And with that kind of success, you know that
poor Tree is in for another day of butchery.

00:03:54.658 --> 00:03:58.718
According to Variety, Blumhouse and Universal
are busy working on a sequel, titled Happy

00:03:58.718 --> 00:03:59.798
Death Day 2U.

00:04:00.238 --> 00:04:04.858
We don't know any real plot details yet,but
returning lead Jessica Rothe told Collider

00:04:04.858 --> 00:04:06.688
that Happy Death Day 2U will be:

00:04:06.778 --> 00:04:10.598
"...a Back to the Future type of genre film
where the sequel joins us right from where

00:04:10.598 --> 00:04:11.378
we left off."

00:04:11.928 --> 00:04:16.238
We'll get to see what fresh horror awaits
our hero on February 14th, 2019.

